total amount of non-military funds Washington has appropriated since 2002 is approximately $100 billion, more than the United States has ever spent to rebuild a country. I further quote, since then, Congress has appropriated another $16.5 billion for reconstruction, and all that has not brought the United States or the Afghan a single sustainable institution or program.

[[00:01:19.300]]
UNIDENTIFIED SPEAKER
As I

[[00:01:19.830]]
