individuals with whom I spoke were incredibly disappointed in Congress. Mr. Speaker, we cannot blame the American people for wanting a vote on this agreement, which will spend billions of American dollars in Afghanistan with little to no accountability over at least the next ten years. This is not a partisan issue. Congressman Jim McGovern and I have signed a letter asking the leadership of both parties for a debate on the expenditure tax dollars to prop up the corrupt nation of Afghanistan. To further explain why this debate is necessary, I will briefly read two more examples from the Money Pit article, and I quote: "The Special Inspector General's Office, widely known as

